# Agent and UI

- One row per message. `tool_calls` hold bounded redacted payloads. `agent_runs` hold status and usage numbers.
- UI pagination is keyset on `sequence_no` (latest page + Load older). LLM context is last N **completed** turns only. Never put the current query in `build_context`.
- Streamlit submits a run and polls with `st.fragment`. Never run LangChain as the only path on the script thread. Never SSE/FastAPI/Celery.
- Worker threads must not call `st.*`. Resolve clients on the script thread and pass them in.
- Chat selector is `?chat=<uuid>` plus New chat. Do not list every chat from Postgres. Sidebar labels use chat title, not the UUID.
- Label sample fallback as synthetic, never Petbarn. Compare UI is a table plus a rating-only chart.
- Chat page: heuristic follow-ups. Sources and charts stay hidden until the user asks (Show buttons or wording in the question). Context/tool tables stay on the Usage page. Sidebar shows total tokens for the open chat.
